From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: da-ai-xian-zun <163512031+da-ai-xian-zun@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:25:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] tb520fu: Lenovo Yoga Pad Pro 12.7 (TB520FU) device port

Everything needed to boot and drive the TB520FU on v7.3.3, as one change:

- SM8650 platform work carried from GUF296's Legion Y700 (TB321FU) tree,
  including its device tree, the built-in DTB carrying only /memory from
  the bootloader, and early boot progress marks (joonhoekim)
- device tree for the TB520FU
- display: dual-DSI DSC bring-up, NT36523/NT36532 panel (Jianhua Lu's
  driver extended), KTZ8866 backlight with high-brightness mode, DP DSC
  and four-pipe 4K@120/144
- input: NT36532 touchscreen and stylus, Lenovo keyboard cover, stylus
  battery and charging through battmgr, Goodix fingerprint SPI sensor
- audio: AW882xx amplifiers, q6apm fixes (capture, lock ordering)
- cameras: GC13A2 front camera driver, WL2868C camera PMIC
- USB-C: PS5169 redriver, UCSI role and DWC3 fixes
- power: EPSS boost frequencies, UFS/PCIe/DSI-PHY clock votes that kept
  the SoC out of low-power states
- TEE: QSEECOM application loading and listeners, 64-bit TA images

The Bluetooth address in the device tree is a placeholder; the build
writes each tablet's own address into the DTB (kernel/scripts/set-bdaddr.sh).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
