+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+/*
+ * Lenovo Yoga Pad Pro 12.7 / Yoga Tab Plus (TB520FU, "Lapis")
+ * Official Pogo-Pin Magnetic Keyboard & Multi-Touch Touchpad Driver
+ * for Mainline Linux (serdev subsystem)
+ *
+ * Clean-room Mainline Linux implementation based on complete binary & BTF
+ * reverse engineering of downstream lenovo_keyboard.ko (Qualcomm SM8650).
+ *
+ * Hardware Architecture (TB520FU / Lapis):
+ *   - UART Controller: Qualcomm GENI UART at 0x00888000 (qupv3_id_1 SE2 / uart10)
+ *     - TX: TLMM GPIO 10 (qup2_se2), RX: TLMM GPIO 11 (qup2_se2)
+ *     - Baudrate: 921600 8N1, no hardware flow control (measured on the device)
+ *   - One-Wire Half-Duplex Multiplex:
+ *     - tx-en-gpios    = <&tlmm 119 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH> (HIGH = Host TX, LOW = Host RX)
+ *     - power-en-gpios = <&tlmm 173 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH> (Pogo-Pin VBUS power enable)
+ *     - plug-gpios     = <&tlmm 198 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>  (LOW when keyboard attached)
+ *     - uart-wake-gpios= <&tlmm 171 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>  (Keyboard wakeup IRQ)
+ *     - pupd-gpios     = <&tlmm 180 ...> is in the vendor tree but belongs to the sensor island; not used
+ *     - lid-gpios      = <&tlmm 200 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>  (Magnetic cover hall sensor)
+ */
+
